dwm - dynamic window manager (briq's custom build)
====================================================

Based on dwm 6.2 with the following patches and customizations.


Patches Applied
---------------
- autostart
- alpha (transparent status bar)
- awesomebar
- decoration hints
- fullscreen
- hide vacant tags
- nametag-prepend (custom tag names)
- noborder
- pertag (per-tag settings)
- restartsig (restart via SIGHUP)
- rotatestack
- swaptags
- vanitygaps
- viewontag
- reorganizetags


Customizations
--------------
- Modkey: Mod4 (Win key)
- Font: fontconfig-based (DejaVu Sans Mono Nerd Font)
- Custom keybindings for volume, brightness, screen capture, lock screen, etc.
- Albert/Rofi launcher integration
- Chrome bound to specific tag
- Touchpad toggle
- No border pixel for single windows
- Custom border colors and gap settings


Bug Fixes
---------
- **pertag curtag UB crash**: Fixed undefined behavior in toggleview when
  `curtag == 0` (the "view all tags" state). The expression `1 << (curtag - 1)`
  evaluates to `1 << -1` when `curtag` is 0, which is undefined behavior in C.
  This caused crashes after prolonged use of `Mod+0` (view all tags) followed
  by toggleview operations. Fixed by checking `curtag == 0` before the shift
  (short-circuit evaluation prevents UB).


Requirements
------------
In order to build dwm you need the Xlib header files.


Installation
------------
Edit config.mk to match your local setup (dwm is installed into
the /usr/local namespace by default).

Afterwards enter the following command to build and install dwm (if
necessary as root):

    make clean install


Running dwm
-----------
Add the following line to your .xinitrc to start dwm using startx:

    exec dwm

In order to connect dwm to a specific display, make sure that
the DISPLAY environment variable is set correctly, e.g.:

    DISPLAY=foo.bar:1 exec dwm

(This will start dwm on display :1 of the host foo.bar.)

In order to display status info in the bar, you can do something
like this in your .xinitrc:

    while xsetroot -name "`date` `uptime | sed 's/.*,//'`"
    do
    	sleep 1
    done &
    exec dwm


Configuration
-------------
The configuration of dwm is done by creating a custom config.h
and (re)compiling the source code.